---
// Flow's Base vs Pro pricing section.
//
// TWO GATES SHAPE THIS COMPONENT, and neither is cosmetic:
//
// 1. ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE is OFF, so NO AMOUNT AND NO BUY BUTTON RENDER. The app
//    does not yet enforce the terms, and a published price the binary
//    contradicts is the worst failure 0127 can produce. What renders instead is
//    the CAPABILITY split, which is true today and enforced at one seam. When the
//    flag flips, the price and the two buy buttons appear with no copy rewrite.
//
// 2. VOCABULARY. The app itself never says "Base" or "Pro" to a user — the
//    shipped badge reads "N days left" and the withdrawal notice says "Subscribe
//    to keep using Flow's AI features". So this page uses Base/Pro as HEADINGS
//    only and quotes the app's own sentences verbatim inside them (the website
//    lane's option 2, recorded in FLOW-GROWTH-CONTRACT.md 2026-08-22 09:15). If
//    the product lane adopts Base/Pro in B2's pill, this needs no change.
//
// NO PRO DAYS COUNTDOWN. The free grant is 10 Pro Days, and a Pro Day is spent
// only on a day the user actually invokes AI, so "10 days free" is FALSE. B2 (the
// tier and remaining pill) is unbuilt, so the grant is described qualitatively or
// not at all — never as a countdown.
import {
  FLOW_BASE_CAPABILITIES,
  FLOW_LAPSE_FACTS,
  FLOW_PRO_CAPABILITIES,
  FLOW_PROMISE,
  FLOW_SPLIT_RULE,
  FLOW_TASTER_NOTE,
  FLOW_WITHDRAWAL_NOTICE,
} from '../../data/flow-pricing.ts';
import { FLOW, formatUsd } from '../../data/commerce.ts';
import { ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE } from '../../data/launch.ts';
import FlowDownloadCta from './FlowDownloadCta.astro';

const monthly = formatUsd(FLOW.monthly.amount);
const annual = formatUsd(FLOW.annual.amount);
const discountPercent = Math.round(FLOW.annualDiscount * 100);
---

<section id="pricing" class="border-t border-border/70 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-label="What is free and what is paid">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent-ink">Base and Pro</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-bold leading-[1.15] sm:text-4xl">
      {FLOW_PROMISE}
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-[1.55] text-text-muted">
      Flow has one line through it, and it sits in one place in the code. Everything that
      reads, writes and organises your documents is free and stays free. {FLOW_SPLIT_RULE}
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2" data-animate-stagger>
      {/* BASE */}
      <article class="of-surface flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6" data-animate>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Base</h3>
          <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent-ink">Free forever</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          The whole document app. No trial, no expiry, no account, and nothing to buy.
          Open a folder of Markdown files and work.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-5 flex-1 space-y-2.5">
          {FLOW_BASE_CAPABILITIES.map((c) => (
            <li class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <span class="font-semibold text-text">{c.label}</span>
              <span class="text-text-dim"> · {c.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </article>

      {/* PRO */}
      <article class="of-surface flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-accent/40 p-6" data-animate>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Pro</h3>
          {ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE ? (
            <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent-ink">
              {monthly}/month · {annual}/year
            </span>
          ) : (
            <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-dim">Subscription</span>
          )}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          Everything in Base, plus Flow's AI. One licence covers one person on as many of
          your own Macs as you like.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-5 flex-1 space-y-2.5">
          {FLOW_PRO_CAPABILITIES.map((c) => (
            <li class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <span class="font-semibold text-text">{c.label}</span>
              <span class="text-text-dim"> · {c.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        {ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE ? (
          <>
            <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-text-muted">
              {monthly} a month, or {annual} a year and save {discountPercent} percent.
            </p>
            {/* The download is the action on BOTH cards, because Base and Pro
                are the same download: you get Base by installing, and the Pro
                Days start you inside the subscription so there is nothing
                separate to buy here. A "Buy now" beside a card the reader cannot
                yet subscribe from would be the working-looking action pointing
                at a missing dependency that the download guard exists to
                prevent. */}
            <div class="mt-5">
              <FlowDownloadCta source="pricing-pro" showCaption={false} />
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-dim">
            Pricing opens when Flow is released
          </p>
        )}
      </article>
    </div>

    {/* The read/produce split. The product lane's 09:55 B11 report calls this the
        real upgrade argument and says it is worth copy rather than a table row:
        a Base user inspects a permanent record of what the AI did and cannot add
        to it. Kept above the lapse block because it explains why Base is not a
        crippled tier. */}
    <div class="of-surface mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6" data-animate>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Base is not a crippled version</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{FLOW_TASTER_NOTE}</p>
    </div>

    {/* The lapse promise. This is the part a reader is actually worried about, so
        it gets its own block rather than a footnote, and it quotes the app. */}
    <div class="of-surface mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6" data-animate>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">If you stop paying, you keep your work</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        When a subscription ends, the AI stops and nothing else does. Flow says so in the
        app, in these words: <span class="text-text">“{FLOW_WITHDRAWAL_NOTICE}”</span>
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {FLOW_LAPSE_FACTS.map((fact) => (
          <li class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{fact}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
      One thing worth being plain about: local models are part of Pro too. Flow can run
      models on your own Mac, and that is still the paid side of the line. What you pay for
      is Flow's approval layer, the routing, the tools, the receipts and the guardrails,
      not the words the model makes.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
